From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thelamer <ryankuba@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:47:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Copy only the blocks of an input picture the caller does
 not mark constant

svt_av1_enc_send_picture copies every input picture whole into the library's pooled luma and
chroma buffers, on the calling thread; a screen encoder knows which 16x16 blocks of a picture are
the frame before's. EbBufferHeaderType.constant_blocks carries that map, and the copy takes only
the other blocks, and those that changed since the buffer it copies into last held the picture:
each pooled buffer, luma and chroma apart, keeps a map of the blocks changed since it was last
written, every push notes the picture's changes in the other buffers' maps, and a resized buffer,
a picture without a map, an input wider than a byte, or a downsampling first pass copies the
picture whole and marks every block of the other buffers.

Every stream comes out bit for bit as with the whole copy, 1920x1080 and 1366x768, constant
quantizer and constant rate, on a still screen, a 256x256 changing box, and a scroll. The copy of
a still 1920x1080 frame took 0.011 ms on the calling thread where it took 0.22, and at 2560x1600
0.025 where it took 0.52; the frame 1.23 ms where it took 1.57 and 2.20 where it took 2.81 on
six logical processors.
